# Pairs with MonotonicVisibility. This is issue #2320's experiment kept as a
# standing check. The registry stops reporting a decision it still holds, and
# instead of saying so (Indeterminate, which the gate hides) it reports the row
# as absent. Absent resolves to InFlight, the gate falls the key through to its
# pre-saga value, and a committed write a reader has already seen reverts. That
# was production's behaviour before AtomicVisibilityGate learnt the
# Indeterminate arm. No clock appears in the trace: the reversion depends only
# on the order of the mask relative to the broadcast.
MODULE: MonotonicVisibilityMaskReportsAbsent
TARGET: MonotonicVisibility
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: reports a masked registry row as absent rather than indeterminate, so a committed key reverts to pre-saga
PERTURBS: RegistryMask

--- FIND
    /\ masked' = [masked EXCEPT ![t] = ~masked[t]]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, vote, decision, terminal, pend, orphanDone, forgotten, revision>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the masked row is reported as absent, which a reader resolves to
\* InFlight, instead of as Indeterminate. No drain ordering protects it.
    /\ forgotten' = [forgotten EXCEPT ![t] = TRUE]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, vote, decision, terminal, pend, orphanDone, masked, revision>>
--- END
